From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:41:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: Add Cirrus Logic CS42L81 driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CS42L81 is an Apple-specific Cirrus Logic codec with integrated
speaker drivers, used in the A9 iPad 5. There is no public datasheet;
the control protocol and the sequences were reconstructed from iOS
16.7.10's AppleCS42L81Audio and AppleCSSPIv2Audio:

 - SPI framing: write 6C page reg 00 val, read 6D page reg 00 xx with
   the value in the 5th byte; device ID 42 A8 1x at 0x01..0x03.
 - Power up (enableAudio) with the codec as the BCLK/LRCK provider,
   sample-rate programming (setSampleRate), the ASP slot maps and the
   power down with a bounded PDN_DONE poll (disableAudio).
 - Speaker route and volume (the CS35L33-style 0.5 dB code with a +0x34
   offset), capped at the board's maximum speaker gain.
 - Capture from the two built-in DMICs (DMIC1A/1B through ADC A/B into
   ASP TX slots 0/1) with iOS's DMIC gain split between the +20 dB boost
   and the digital volume.
 - Headphone route with iOS's speaker-to-headphone change, the HP gain
   split and the charge pump kept off while the driver settles.

Speakers and the stereo microphone work on J71t. The headphone path
follows iOS but has not been validated; the codec's plug-detect status
bit is not known yet, so userspace selects speakers or headphones with
the "Output Select" control.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux ce134b9f, 58b8042d and the squash
 3e47c1c2 (J71t ledger 10.6), omarchy-ipad5 patches/audio 0002/0014 and
 capture-jack. Reviewed to mainline practice: dropped the jack status
 survey (jack_poll_ms, jack_reg, jack_mask, jack_invert), the debugfs
 register and jack files, the dmic_bit7 parameter (bit 7 is always set,
 as iOS's default) and the hs-switch GPIOs that were only read for
 diagnostics. Speakers and headphones are a DAPM demux instead of pins
 switched by a jack nobody could report yet. Maximum speaker gain from
 cirrus,speaker-max-gain; stereo speakers only; MCLK required; no
 dev_info messages.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig   |   11 +
 sound/soc/codecs/Makefile  |    2 +
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l81.c | 1154 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1167 insertions(+)
